{
  "title": [
    "sidechain~"
  ],
  "description": "sidechain compression",
  "origin": "ELSE",
  "categories": [
    "Effects",
    "Mixing and Routing"
  ],
  "inlets": [
    {
      "messages": [
        {
          "type": "float/signals",
          "description": "input signal"
        }
      ],
      "repeat": false
    },
    {
      "messages": [
        {
          "type": "float/signals",
          "description": "control signal"
        }
      ],
      "repeat": false
    }
  ],
  "outlets": [
    {
      "messages": [
        {
          "type": "signals",
          "description": "ducked signal alone or mixed with control signal"
        }
      ],
      "repeat": false
    }
  ],
  "arguments": [
    {
      "type": "float",
      "description": "threshold in dB",
      "default": "-60"
    },
    {
      "type": "float",
      "description": "attenuation ratio",
      "default": "1"
    },
    {
      "type": "float",
      "description": "attack time in ms",
      "default": "10"
    },
    {
      "type": "float",
      "description": "release time in ms",
      "default": "10"
    }
  ],
  "flags": [
    {
      "name": "-mix",
      "description": "mixes with control signal"
    }
  ],
  "methods": [
    {
      "type": "thresh <float>",
      "description": "sets threshold in dB"
    },
    {
      "type": "ratio <float>",
      "description": "sets attenuation ratio"
    },
    {
      "type": "attack <float>",
      "description": "sets attack time in ms"
    },
    {
      "type": "release <float>",
      "description": "sets release time in ms"
    },
    {
      "type": "mix <float>",
      "description": "nonzero mixes with control signal"
    }
  ],
  "body": "[sidechain~] is an abstraction that performs sidechain compression, so it attenuates an input signal according to the level of a control signal (a.k.a. 'key signal' or side chain input). Usually you mix the compressed signal with the side chain input, and there's a flag for that. There's support for multichannels."
}